+### GET `/channel-groups/:id/usage-credit-routing`
+
+Returns `{usageCreditPolicy, accounts}` for this group. Optional `model` selects model-specific quota windows. Account entries contain `use` (`plan`, `credits`, `unknown`, `exhausted`, `blocked`), `eligible`, `reason` and `policy`. Under `never`, credit-only and unknown accounts keep their funding `use` and return `eligible: false`, `reason: "credit_policy_never"`.
+
+v8 channel-group create/update and read responses accept/expose `usage_credit_policy`: `last_resort` (default) or `never`. The strictest applicable server-owned group policy governs an authenticated client key. Known plan quota precedes credits, then unknown funding, before session affinity. `never` admits only fresh proven plan quota. A funding refusal requests a bounded, coalesced normal quota collection. A spending guarantee still requires disabling extra usage at the vendor because observations can change between collection and a request.
+
+v8 quota detail responses include nullable `usage_credits`: `state`, optional decimal-string `balance`, source `observed_at`/`expires_at`, Codex `allowed`/`limit_reached`/`has_credits`/`unlimited`, and optional Claude `extra_usage` with `enabled`, `monthly_cap` (`limited`, `unlimited`, `unknown`) and `used_ratio`. `credit_blocked` preserves explicit zero, disabled or exhausted evidence. Claude caps are not wallets; currency and scale are unproven, so no money amount is published. `reset_credits` remains separate. Older rows without these facts are unknown until collection.
+
 ### DELETE `/channel-groups/:id`
 
 Soft-deletes the group and its details, and atomically removes its ID from API key `channels` and model group detail `channels`, including soft-deleted records. Other bindings, key identity, and user ownership are preserved. Removing the last API key channel binding makes credential selection unrestricted by that key; removing the last model-detail channel binding restores inheritance from the key. A config event is published when bindings change, and the local runtime config is refreshed. Disabled groups are not removed.
